tem architecture and data flow."},{"id":"w21-topic04","week_number":21,"kind":"topic","position":4,"label":"Design PostgreSQL schemas and vector storage."},{"id":"w21-topic05","week_number":21,"kind":"topic","position":5,"label":"Define API contracts and service boundaries."},{"id":"w21-topic06","week_number":21,"kind":"topic","position":6,"label":"Design document ingestion and RAG retrieval."},{"id":"w21-topic07","week_number":21,"kind":"topic","position":7,"label":"Design tools, n8n integration, and approval paths."},{"id":"w21-topic08","week_number":21,"kind":"topic","position":8,"label":"Define evaluation criteria and test data."},{"id":"w21-topic09","week_number":21,"kind":"topic","position":9,"label":"Break the implementation into testable milestones."},{"id":"w21-practice","week_number":21,"kind":"practice","position":100,"label":"Write a short technical specification before implementation."},{"id":"w21-acceptance","week_number":21,"kind":"acceptance","position":101,"label":"A scoped capstone specification connects each feature to a business need, test strategy, and measurable outcome."},{"id":"w22-topic01","week_number":22,"kind":"topic","position":1,"label":"Input and output validation at system boundaries."},{"id":"w22-topic02","week_number":22,"kind":"topic","position":2,"label":"Edge cases, empty data, and malformed inputs."},{"id":"w22-topic03","week_number":22,"kind":"topic","position":3,"label":"Duplicate requests and idempotent operations."},{"id":"w22-topic04","week_number":22,"kind":"topic","position":4,"label":"Retry limits, timeouts, and recovery paths."},{"id":"w22-topic05","week_number":22,"kind":"topic","position":5,"label":"RAG grounding, citation correctness, and abstention."},{"id":"w22-topic06","week_number":22,"kind":"topic","position":6,"label":"Tool permissions, approval checks, and auditability."},{"id":"w22-topic07","week_number":22,"kind":"topic","position":7,"label":"Evaluation dataset of 100+ cases."},{"id":"w22-topic08","week_numb